{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795222,"nonce":"8lsCLrpG9qv6Tv+vtlLbA1Z7a5w=","title":"Prototype native WebRTC, device capture and media-process transport","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P0\n\nScope\nEvaluate maintained native WebRTC/capture/audio stacks for macOS, Windows and Linux with Cloudflare SFU interoperability. Prototype microphone/camera/window capture, OS permission flows, codec negotiation, hardware acceleration and Ashui video presentation. Design a dedicated media process plus bounded control/frame transport and release ownership; never marshal raw frames as JSON/base64 or pass process-local pointers. Compare the native path with a browser/RealtimeKit proof of concept and record supported/unsupported targets and build/license notices.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nA measured feasibility result demonstrates one audio/video round trip and crash/stop recovery on each claimed target, or explicitly records blockers. Report editor/helper/aggregate CPU, memory, GPU resources and latency. Device removal and denied permissions leave editing alive. The selected library/IPC approach is justified before full call UI work begins.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}